WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.585
- Ah, you got it, all the way.

00:00:02.585 --> 00:00:04.629
Yeah! Good job.

00:00:04.629 --> 00:00:07.424
Get out of the studio.
This is blasphemy!

00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:11.469
- Jack Boys!
E-A-G-L-E-S! Eagles!

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:16.141
♪♪♪

00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:18.309
Welcome to
"Simms &amp; Lefkoe," everybody.

00:00:18.309 --> 00:00:21.312
We're not in the studio,
and we're dressed like elves.

00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:22.772
- Hey. What up, elf?
- Good to see you.

00:00:22.772 --> 00:00:24.899
And this: Who is this, Simms?

00:00:24.899 --> 00:00:28.153
- This is jolly old Saint Nick.
- Show 'em who you are.

00:00:28.153 --> 00:00:29.696
- Big reveal.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.531
- Da-da-da!
- Oh, there he is!

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.993
We're back with the main man
himself, San Darnold

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:37.120
and we're here
at the Livingston Mall.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.913
Today it's not Santa Claus.

00:00:38.913 --> 00:00:41.249
- Look at the tape on his lip.
That's what I'm lookin' at.

00:00:41.249 --> 00:00:43.334
- It's "Samta" Claus.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:49.758
♪♪♪

00:00:49.758 --> 00:00:56.139
♪♪♪

00:00:56.139 --> 00:00:59.434
- Ho, ho, ho!

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:02.062
- Santa, we got Joey here.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.522
- Oh, give me a high-five, buddy. Oh, sit right here.
- Joey!

00:01:04.522 --> 00:01:06.816
- Tell me what you want
for Christmas this year.

00:01:06.816 --> 00:01:09.736
- A Nintendo Switch.
- Oh, that's a great game

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.571
I've heard,
from all the kids.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.865
What do you guys want
for Christmas this year?

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:16.785
- I want a Puppy Surprise.

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:18.536
- A Puppy Surprise?

00:01:18.536 --> 00:01:20.538
- A Nerf gun.
- A Nerf ball?

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:22.457
- A Nerf gun.
- A Nerf gun.

00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:24.250
- We definitely
have a lot of those.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.878
- We have a lot of those, right?
- We do.

00:01:26.878 --> 00:01:29.172
- Santa, we got Stephen here.
- Ho, ho, ho, Stephen.

00:01:29.172 --> 00:01:31.007
What do you want
for Christmas this year?

00:01:31.007 --> 00:01:32.759
- A Saquon Barkley jersey.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.054
- Saquon Barkley jersey?

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:38.223
What do you want
for Christmas this year?

00:01:38.223 --> 00:01:40.600
- Saquon Barkley jersey.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.977
- Saquon.
Do you watch football?

00:01:42.977 --> 00:01:44.646
-Yeah.
- Who's your favorite team?

00:01:44.646 --> 00:01:47.148
- Packers.
- Hey, buddy. What's your name?

00:01:47.148 --> 00:01:49.317
- Blake.
- Blake, good to meet you.

00:01:49.317 --> 00:01:52.821
- Ooh, I like your jersey, Blake.
- Sit right here, bud.

00:01:52.821 --> 00:01:54.948
Oh, yeah, that's a really cool jersey you got on there.
- Yeah.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.533
- Who's your favorite player
on the Jets?

00:01:56.533 --> 00:01:59.828
- Sam Darnold or Jamal Adams.
- Or Jamal.

00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:02.622
I think maybe one day you'll be
able to meet one of those guys.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.290
Maybe next year, though.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.459
- Santa's my cousin.
- He's your cousin?

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.628
That's cool. Good family.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.755
Coolest name
we've had yet, Santa.

00:02:10.755 --> 00:02:12.257
- What is it?
- Chris.

00:02:12.257 --> 00:02:15.135
- Oh, Chris.
- I like that name, kinda.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.428
What do you want
for Christmas this year, buddy?

00:02:17.428 --> 00:02:19.430
- A skateboard.
- A skateboard.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.432
- Do you like the Jets?
- Yes.

00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:23.226
- Yeah?

00:02:23.226 --> 00:02:26.855
So, Santa used to play football
at North Pole High School

00:02:26.855 --> 00:02:30.150
and we want him
to throw you a pass.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.110
- A little bit further than that.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:35.196
♪♪♪

00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:36.656
Nice catch.
- Good catch, Chris.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.950
Santa was a little off-target.
- Yeah.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:41.244
Yeah, you had to go up
and get that one, didn't you?

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:42.704
- We were wondering if anyone

00:02:42.704 --> 00:02:45.123
wanted to catch passes
from Santa Claus.

00:02:45.123 --> 00:02:47.208
[Children shouting]

00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:49.377
- Let's see what you got, Santa.

00:02:49.377 --> 00:02:52.338
♪♪♪

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:55.175
- [Cheering]
- Oh! Ho, ho!

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.677
- Santa can really throw!

00:02:57.677 --> 00:03:00.138
♪♪♪

00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:02.223
- Oh!
- Oh!

00:03:02.223 --> 00:03:04.642
- Oh!

00:03:04.642 --> 00:03:06.811
- Oh. You got it, all the way.

00:03:06.811 --> 00:03:08.521
- Yeah!
- Good job.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.273
- The reindeer told me

00:03:10.273 --> 00:03:12.275
that it's time for you
to go to the bathroom.

00:03:12.275 --> 00:03:13.860
Is it true?
- Yes, it is.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.404
- I know. Santa's gotta go
to the bathroom.

00:03:16.404 --> 00:03:18.448
- Santa can't hold it in.

00:03:18.448 --> 00:03:24.454
♪♪♪

00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:26.623
- I don't know
what happened to Santa.

00:03:26.623 --> 00:03:30.710
But his friend came, and
I want you to meet him, OK?

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:35.632
I wanna introduce you
to the starting quarterback

00:03:35.632 --> 00:03:41.387
of the New York Jets,
Sam Darnold!

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.097
[Cheering]

00:03:43.097 --> 00:03:44.807
- High-five, buddy.

00:03:44.807 --> 00:03:47.644
- Good game against Buffalo!

00:03:47.644 --> 00:03:49.604
- Oh, thank you so much.
Gimme a high-five.

00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:54.317
- Ohhh J-E-T-S!

00:03:54.317 --> 00:03:56.527
Jets, Jets, Jets!

00:03:56.527 --> 00:03:58.655
[Camera shutter clicking]

00:03:58.655 --> 00:04:01.991
♪♪♪

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:03.618
- Samta Claus!
- Samta Claus!

00:04:03.618 --> 00:04:05.995
- Did you enjoy being an elf?
- I did. I really did.

00:04:05.995 --> 00:04:07.538
- Yeah?
- Yeah, it was good.

00:04:07.538 --> 00:04:09.749
You were a cute little elf,
though, real cute.

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.292
- Thanks.
- Yeah. Way to help out Santa.

00:04:11.292 --> 00:04:13.086
- You know what?
I appreciate that.

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.797
I'm gonna take that compliment
and not even go back to ya.

00:04:15.797 --> 00:04:17.423
One person that doesn't
like Christmas: Bill Belichick.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:21.261
- Came out and said—
- How dare you say that to him?

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.887
- "Christmas comes at
an inconvenient time

00:04:22.887 --> 00:04:24.639
right in the middle
of football season"

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:26.349
which is Bill Belichick to a T.

00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:28.101
- Right.
- In fact, if he said

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.144
he liked Christmas,
I would've been disappointed.

00:04:30.144 --> 00:04:32.146
- Well, he's a curmudgeon.
We know that.

00:04:32.146 --> 00:04:34.732
- I can just see him, like,
pretending to open up gifts

00:04:34.732 --> 00:04:37.068
and going, "This is great"

00:04:37.068 --> 00:04:39.028
but, like, actually having
play calls in the gift wrapping paper.

00:04:39.028 --> 00:04:40.488
- No, this is all just getting
in the way right now, OK?

00:04:40.488 --> 00:04:42.240
He's tryin' to get ready
for the playoffs

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.574
and he doesn't wanna worry

00:04:43.574 --> 00:04:44.993
about who's naughty
and who's nice.

00:04:44.993 --> 00:04:47.745
- Do you think Bill Belichick
likes New Year's?

00:04:47.745 --> 00:04:49.831
- Uh, well, I don't think
he cares because

00:04:49.831 --> 00:04:51.874
as my New England friends
always joke

00:04:51.874 --> 00:04:54.002
when the playoffs start,
they always go

00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:56.921
"Regular season's starting
for us," which is pretty true.

00:04:56.921 --> 00:04:59.632
- Damn. I'm so jealous
of Patriots fans.

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:02.468
So, that's an inconvenient time
for Bill Belichick

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:05.138
but I wanna talk
about inconvenient truths.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:08.766
♪♪♪

00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:10.101
I'm gonna give the team.

00:05:10.101 --> 00:05:11.853
You tell me the inconvenient
truth about this playoff team

00:05:11.853 --> 00:05:13.980
and what can hold them back.
- Gotcha.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.606
- The New Orleans Saints.
- The New Orleans Saints.

00:05:15.606 --> 00:05:17.275
I'll tell you one of
the inconvenient truths there.

00:05:17.275 --> 00:05:18.735
- What's the excuse
they've been leaning on?

00:05:18.735 --> 00:05:20.028
- Well, I will say this.

00:05:20.028 --> 00:05:21.654
I think one of
the inconvenient truths

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.448
and it's been exposed
a little bit

00:05:23.448 --> 00:05:26.075
is Drew Brees and what he can
bring to the Saints offense.

00:05:26.075 --> 00:05:28.119
I know. We're gonna
open up a can of worms here.

00:05:28.119 --> 00:05:30.079
- What do you want? What do
you want, Who Dat Nation?

00:05:30.079 --> 00:05:31.789
- But we talk about offenses
all the time, right?
- Yes!

00:05:31.789 --> 00:05:34.000
- How great offenses make you defend the whole field.
- Sure.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:37.712
- But he's not— at this age,
39 years old, he's not capable

00:05:37.712 --> 00:05:40.381
of scrambling out of the pocket,
making plays that way.

00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:42.675
- Monday against Carolina,
when the rush got there

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:44.344
the play was over.
- Exactly right.

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:47.305
He's not gonna make
any physically demanding plays

00:05:47.305 --> 00:05:49.515
that we're gonna go,
"Whoa, there was nobody open

00:05:49.515 --> 00:05:51.100
the protection
wasn't that great

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.852
and he still made it happen."

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:56.814
And, hey, listen. He throws
the ball shorter downfield.

00:05:56.814 --> 00:05:58.441
He's tied with Eli Manning

00:05:58.441 --> 00:06:00.234
for 28th in football
in yards in the air.

00:06:00.234 --> 00:06:02.570
- Intended air yards—
him and Eli tied.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:05.323
- Yes, so, again, they can win the Super Bowl with him.
- Yes.

00:06:05.323 --> 00:06:08.451
- But there is little issues
with his game

00:06:08.451 --> 00:06:10.787
and when you see teams
take away their screens

00:06:10.787 --> 00:06:12.372
and things like that

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.624
that offense doesn't work
as smoothly because nobody's

00:06:14.624 --> 00:06:16.918
scared of Drew Brees
throwing bombs over their head.

00:06:16.918 --> 00:06:19.796
- There's one team that everybody is piling on right now—
- Yeah.

00:06:19.796 --> 00:06:22.090
- Cuz they're excited they no longer have a bye.
- Right.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.633
- The Patriots.
- Ooh.

00:06:23.633 --> 00:06:25.218
- I'm still scared
of the Patriots.

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:27.011
- Yes, you should be.
- Just gonna put that out there.

00:06:27.011 --> 00:06:28.513
But what is their
inconvenient truth?

00:06:28.513 --> 00:06:31.516
- Their inconvenient truth
is that Gronk

00:06:31.516 --> 00:06:34.060
is no longer the greatest
mismatch in football.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:35.436
That has ended.
- Wow.

00:06:35.436 --> 00:06:38.064
- Gronk is no longer
holding the trophy

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.857
as the best tight end
in the game.

00:06:39.857 --> 00:06:41.734
And I would even argue
that he's not

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:44.070
even Brady's go-to guy
all the time.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.781
I think there's been big moments
during the year where he's gone

00:06:46.781 --> 00:06:48.324
"I'm gonna go
to Josh Gordon here.

00:06:48.324 --> 00:06:50.034
I trust him in this situation."

00:06:50.034 --> 00:06:52.203
And since Josh Gordon's
been there, he's been targeted

00:06:52.203 --> 00:06:53.996
more than any other receiver
on their team.

00:06:53.996 --> 00:06:57.041
- I want a real truth.
- But yes, Gronk has lost a step.

00:06:57.041 --> 00:06:59.710
I do think he's lost his
intensity, and I

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.838
don't think— hey, there's a reason
New England was rumored

00:07:01.838 --> 00:07:03.965
to be trying to trade him
in the offseason.

00:07:03.965 --> 00:07:05.967
I think they saw a few,
you know

00:07:05.967 --> 00:07:09.637
dents in the armor here
that were about to come about.

00:07:09.637 --> 00:07:11.180
- A few more dents in the armor.
- Yeah.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:14.183
- L.A. Rams. This offense has been struggling.
- Yeah.

00:07:14.183 --> 00:07:16.060
- What's the inconvenient truth
about the Rams?

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:17.937
- People are gonna point
to Jared Goff, right?

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:19.647
- They are.
- Who's been in Strugglesville.

00:07:19.647 --> 00:07:21.065
I mean, yes.
- One touchdown the last three weeks.

00:07:21.065 --> 00:07:22.608
- It's not been perfect.
OK, I get that.

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:23.901
So he deserves
some of the blame

00:07:23.901 --> 00:07:25.611
but the real inconvenient truth

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.572
is the interior part of their offensive line.
- Really?

00:07:27.572 --> 00:07:30.158
- They got big-time issues
there, and that's really

00:07:30.158 --> 00:07:32.910
the biggest reason you've seen
all three of their losses.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.997
Sheldon Rankins whupped them
for the Saints, OK?

00:07:35.997 --> 00:07:37.415
Eddie Goldman and Akiem Hicks

00:07:37.415 --> 00:07:38.958
whupped them when the
Bears beat them, right?

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.585
- Dominated.
- Fletcher Cox and your Eagles

00:07:40.585 --> 00:07:42.420
whupped their butt
this past week.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.255
- I don't know how that happened.
- That's the inconvenient truth.

00:07:44.255 --> 00:07:46.424
Now they can't win any of those
battles on the inside.

00:07:46.424 --> 00:07:48.426
Their running game's
not working, and, of course

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:50.094
pressure is getting
into Goff's face

00:07:50.094 --> 00:07:51.429
and he's not as sharp, either.

00:07:51.429 --> 00:07:53.514
- I have one more inconvenient truth
- One more—

00:07:53.514 --> 00:07:55.766
- And it's me to you.
- Oh, gosh.

00:07:55.766 --> 00:07:58.644
It's inconvenient that I gotta
work with you on a daily basis.

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:01.314
- All right, well, now I'm not
afraid to say it anymore.

00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:04.525
I can't believe I'm saying this.
- What?
- He's over my shoulder.

00:08:04.525 --> 00:08:06.694
I don't think Aaron Rodgers
is the best quarterback

00:08:06.694 --> 00:08:08.196
in the NFL anymore.

00:08:08.196 --> 00:08:10.531
- You sound like my son Phillip,
who last week

00:08:10.531 --> 00:08:12.992
was watching Patrick Mahomes
on Thursday night and said

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:15.536
"Mahomes is better than
Aaron Rodgers now, Dad."

00:08:15.536 --> 00:08:18.331
- Look, I'm just happy
that one Simms in the family

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:20.541
has some sense,
but I think that Patrick Mahomes

00:08:20.541 --> 00:08:22.585
is far and away better
than Aaron Rodgers.

00:08:22.585 --> 00:08:24.754
- Get out of the studio.
Get out of the studio.

00:08:24.754 --> 00:08:26.380
- We have a shrine.
- This is blasphemy!

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.633
- I think he is.
- He's the second shrine in here.

00:08:28.633 --> 00:08:29.926
Blasphemy. Get out.
I don't even know who you are.

00:08:29.926 --> 00:08:31.928
- I think that that should
become the primary shrine.

00:08:31.928 --> 00:08:33.930
- Where is Adam Lefkoe? Who—
what—where did my host go?

00:08:33.971 --> 00:08:36.599
- I'm just saying that—
- He doesn't have Tyreek Hill

00:08:36.599 --> 00:08:39.143
he didn't have Kareem Hunt,
he doesn't have Andy Reid

00:08:39.143 --> 00:08:42.647
he doesn't have Sammy Watkins,
he doesn't have Travis Kelce.

00:08:42.647 --> 00:08:45.399
♪ Aaron Rodgers,
you're still the greatest ♪

00:08:45.399 --> 00:08:48.444
♪ But even the greatest
needs help sometimes ♪

00:08:48.444 --> 00:08:51.364
- I just— I'm not saying
he's worse than two.

00:08:51.364 --> 00:08:53.699
- Yeah.
- I'm just sayin' he's not one.

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:55.910
- It's the first year—
I'm not gonna lie

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:57.495
I've had moments where I've—
- Say it. Say it.

00:08:57.495 --> 00:08:59.163
- Nope. I've had moments
where I've gone

00:08:59.163 --> 00:09:01.165
"Huh, this is getting
kinda close."

00:09:01.165 --> 00:09:02.875
- You said, "Huh."
- I said, "Huh.

00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:04.377
This is getting kinda close."
- Wow.

00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:05.795
- But I'm still not gonna
give him the nod yet.

00:09:05.795 --> 00:09:07.630
- The best part
that it was Phillip

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:09.632
is I can keep "Simms &amp; Lefkoe"
and just replace you with him.

00:09:09.632 --> 00:09:11.300
- Oh, thanks.
- I love that.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:13.177
- Thanks a lot.
- Me and an eight-year-old

00:09:13.177 --> 00:09:15.555
comin' next week.

00:09:15.555 --> 00:09:19.016
- Hey, I'm Chris Johnson,
aka CJ2K

00:09:19.016 --> 00:09:22.478
and you're watching
"Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:09:22.478 --> 00:09:25.731
- "Somebody &amp; Lefkoe."
One second, one second.

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:27.817
All right,
just wanna make sure

00:09:27.817 --> 00:09:30.111
Allie's not here to surprise me,
not today

00:09:30.111 --> 00:09:33.322
because I found him
back where he should be

00:09:33.322 --> 00:09:36.826
in his newspaper stand,
pickin' winners.

00:09:36.826 --> 00:09:39.495
Enough losers, Allie.
Get back on track!

00:09:43.165 --> 00:09:45.001
Chiefs-Chargers.

00:09:45.001 --> 00:09:48.379
I'm at home, and I'm goin',
"Man, another win by Allie."

00:09:48.379 --> 00:09:52.008
Instead of 7-2, you're now 6-3
because of Philip Rivers.

00:09:52.008 --> 00:09:54.010
What does that do to your heart

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:55.761
to know that you took an L on
the hands of Philip last week?

00:09:55.761 --> 00:09:56.971
to know that you took an L on
the hands of Philip last week?

00:09:56.971 --> 00:09:58.347
to know that you took an L on
the hands of Philip last week?

00:09:58.347 --> 00:09:58.389
- I think it hurts me more
that he could've been a Giant.

00:09:58.389 --> 00:10:00.975
- I think it hurts me more
that he could've been a Giant.

00:10:00.975 --> 00:10:03.102
[Laughing]
- Right? Wow.

